prompts:
Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: production 2.5D medieval dark-apocalypse RPG sprite animation sheet, genuinely transparent RGBA PNG.
Input image 1 is ONLY an identity and material reference: use the gray hooded sword-and-lantern player in its top-left cell for row 1, and the mutated hooded player with the long pale bony claw in its third-row second cell for row 2. Input image 2 is ONLY a rendering style and camera reference; use its first character identity, not its layout. Create a NEW player-only ranged attack sheet, not a walking sheet.
REQUIRED EXACT LAYOUT: exactly SIX equal-width columns and TWO equal-height rows, twelve complete isolated full-body characters. Wide 3:1 canvas, preferably 1536 x 512. Every figure must be VERY SMALL inside its own cell, contained within the MIDDLE 60 PERCENT of BOTH cell width and cell height. Leave at least 20 percent of cell width transparent on each side, and 20 percent of cell height transparent above and below each character. This padding is functional: maintain wide EMPTY TRANSPARENT vertical and horizontal gutters at ALL uniform cell boundaries and the entire outer canvas border. Do not enlarge the figures to fill the sheet. No figure, weapon, sleeve, cape, lantern, claw, or shadow may approach or cross a cell boundary.
All twelve figures face screen-right in exactly the same fixed three-quarter isometric view. Same realistic natural proportions, lighting, camera scale, cloth, leather, metal details and identity within each row. Full body visible with identical standing body height within each row, torso centered on the cell center, feet grounded on exactly the same baseline in every frame. Boots stay planted throughout the attack; no stepping, jumping, hovering or vertical bobbing. Keep head and torso size constant. Sparse slight cloth motion only.
TOP ROW, gray hood player: retain dark gray weathered cloak, layered brown leather armor and belts, boots, lowered steel sword in the same hand, and small brass warm-glowing lantern in the other hand, matching the references. Attack is a magical ranged release using the lantern arm toward screen-right; the lowered sword is retained throughout.
BOTTOM ROW, mutated player: retain dark gray hood and ragged cloak, brown leather torso, dark boots, red eyes, and one pale elongated bony thorned claw, matching image 1. Attack is a ranged casting thrust of the large claw toward screen-right.
Each row has a readable SIX-FRAME attack sequence from left to right:
frame 1: arm already thrust forward in the instant of release, torso slightly forward;
frame 2: full horizontal arm/claw extension toward screen-right;
frame 3: follow-through, shoulder and torso twist with extended arm beginning to settle;
frame 4: recoil, elbow visibly bent and hand pulled toward torso;
frame 5: hand/lantern/claw lowering toward hip, torso returning upright;
frame 6: relaxed settled neutral idle matching original standing outfit.
The arm and shoulder silhouettes MUST differ visibly across all six frames. Show a coherent single attack recovery, not six identical static poses. Do not add projectile, fireball, smoke, rays, or effects: projectiles are rendered separately by game code. Warm lantern remains small. No floor, ground shadows, grid lines, labels, numbers, text, watermark, background, checkerboard, weapons swapping, clothing swaps, extra characters, decorative frames. Preserve actual transparent alpha.
